    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "RABAUL\nFINSCHAFEN\nLAE\nPORT MORESBY •\nCAIRNS\nNew Guinea\nBIRD OF PARADISE SERVICE\nand Islands Services\nNOUMEA - SUVA - VILA - ESPIRITU SANTO\nNORFOLK ISLAND - - LORD HOWE ISLAND\nThe Qantas New Guinea Service (known as\nthe \"Bird of Paradise\" Service) leaves\nSydney three times weekly. Two of these\nservices terminate at Lae, and the third goes\non to Rabaul Passengers are also carried\nto and from North Queensland ports.\nA Qantas air service links Noumea and Suva\nwith Sydney. From Noumea a service extends\nto Vila and Espiritu Santo.\nA Norfolk Island service is flown by speedy\nLancastrian aircraft every fortnight from\nSydney, and a charter service is flown by a\nQantas Catalina between Sydney and Lord\nHowe Island once weekly.\nTOWNSVILLE\nSUVA\nROCKHAMPTON\nNORFOLK ISLAND\nBRISBANE •\ncean\nковкія\nLORD HOWE ISLAND\nSYDNEY O\nS",
      "Qantas Empire Airways",
      "AND\nBIRD OF PARADISE\nSERVICE\nQantas Empire Airways"
    ],
